 // SPDX-License-Identifier: (GPL-2.0-only OR BSD-2-Clause)
 /*
- * OPPO A3 (2018) - PADM00 / PADT00 / CPH1837
- * MediaTek MT6771 (Helio P60)
+ * OPPO A3 (PADT00, MediaTek MT6771 / Helio P60) board device tree.
  *
- * Measured facts used here (see linux/docs/mt6771-facts.md):
- *   RAM            : 4 GiB at 0x40000000  (/proc/iomem: System RAM ends at
- *                    0x13fffefff; MemTotal 3,744,292 kB)
- *   Framebuffer    : 0x7d170000, 16 MiB  (chosen/atag,videolfb in the DT that
- *                    LK handed to the stock kernel)
- *   Panel          : oppo17331_dpt_jdi_nt36672_1080p_dsi_vdo, 1080x2280,
- *                    DSI video mode, 60.13 fps (/proc/cmdline lcm= parameter)
- *   ramoops        : 0x54410000, ~896 KiB  (persistent_ram regions in
- *                    /proc/iomem -- the vendor kernel's ram_console/pstore)
+ * PROVENANCE
+ * ----------
+ * This file is the *authoritative* board description for the mainline port and
+ * is what `make ARCH=arm64 dtbs` compiles. It was produced by decompiling the
+ * known-good DTB that the port actually boots with, so that the source tree
+ * reproduces that exact hardware description:
  *
- * Deliberate omissions for this first (M1a) boot test:
- *   - no modem/CCIF/MD reserved-memory: we do not do cellular (user decision
- *     K2), the RAM is handed back to the kernel.
- *   - no clock / pinctrl / power-domain / display-engine nodes: without a
- *     clock driver nothing gets gated, which is exactly what we want while
- *     the panel is still driven by whatever LK set up.
+ *     dtc -I dtb -O dts -o mt6771-oppo-a3.dts stock-a3-hw.dtb
+ *
+ * The DTB it came from started life as the vendor (Android 4.14) device tree
+ * and was then patched for mainline:
+ *
+ *   USB (mtu3 + tphy)
+ *     - usb3@11200000: compatible -> "mediatek,mtu3"
+ *     - reg: mac size 0x3000 -> 0x2e00, because the vendor layout puts the
+ *       "ippc" window *inside* the "mac" window and mainline requests both
+ *       with devm_request_mem_region(), which fails with -EBUSY on overlap
+ *     - drop clocks/clock-names/extcon (mainline has no MT6771 clock driver)
+ *     - dr_mode = "peripheral" (get_ssusb_rscs() needs "vbus" otherwise)
+ *     - vusb33-supply -> fixed regulator; mediatek,u3p-dis-msk = <1> (USB2 only)
+ *     - usb0phy@11f40000 -> "mediatek,generic-tphy-v2" with a usb-phy@0 child;
+ *       phys = <&usb-phy@0 PHY_TYPE_USB2> (phandle on the CHILD: mtk_phy_xlate
+ *       matches by child node, and the 2nd cell is the phy *type*, not an index)
+ *
+ *   eMMC (mtk-sd)
+ *     - msdc@11230000: compatible -> "mediatek,mt6771-mmc"
+ *     - clocks -> clk26m for "hclk" and clk_msdcpll (400 MHz) for "source":
+ *       the divider is derived from the ASSUMED source rate, so claiming
+ *       26 MHz while the hardware runs from msdcpll overclocks the card and
+ *       produces I/O errors
+ *     - vmmc-supply -> fixed 3.3 V regulator (without it mmc core leaves
+ *       ocr_avail at 0 and every attach fails with "no support for card's volts")
+ *     - high-speed caps removed for bring-up (HS400 needs 200 MHz + tuning)
+ *
+ *   Display
+ *     - simple-framebuffer at 0x77440000, stride 0x1100 (1088 px)
+ *
+ * Do not edit this file by hand to "fix" a boot problem: change the patching
+ * script (linux/script/a3-patch-*.py), regenerate the DTB, and re-decompile.
+ * Keeping it self-contained means the build needs no vendor headers.
  */
 
